# Sesh Helpers — start here

Read [`docs/001_CLANKER_INIT.md`](../../docs/001_CLANKER_INIT.md) first, then the docs
index [`docs/README.md`](../../docs/README.md), then the task-specific doc. Docs record
intended contracts; running code is evidence too. Verify docs against the code before
changing behavior instead of trusting stale text.

## What this project is

Helper overlays for the Sesh Sofa show. Static HTML/JS/CSS per app, dependency-light,
**no build step and no CI** — the repo root is the webroot, deployed to GitHub Pages at
`https://helpers.seshsofa.nl/`. License AGPL-3.0.

| Path | What lives there |
|------|------------------|
| `spotsmoke/`, `seshbanner/`, `trbanner/` | Helper apps (OBS Browser Sources) |
| `abs/` | ABS — Animated Background System (OBS backdrops; no shared themes) |
| `themes/` | Shared overlay themes — [`docs/THEMES.md`](../../docs/THEMES.md) |
| `*/notes.md` | Operator setup + the complete URL parameter contract per app |
| `index.html` | Landing page listing every app |

## Working principles

- **Minimal scope** — smallest correct change. No drive-by refactors.
- **No over-engineering** — no abstractions for one-liners, no speculative error
  handling for impossible edges.
- **Match existing conventions** — read surrounding code and docs before inventing a
  new pattern.
- **Document what you build** — if you add a mechanism, write down how it works.
- **Tests only when meaningful** — cover real behavior, not obvious trivia.
- **Honesty over completeness** — write "TBD" rather than fabricated detail.

## Hard rules

- **Never commit unless explicitly asked.** Mortal meat bags control git history.
- New helper app: own directory, linked from `index.html`, repo map in
  `docs/001_CLANKER_INIT.md` updated.
- New doc: add it to [`docs/README.md`](../../docs/README.md), and to
  `001_CLANKER_INIT.md` if it is essential onboarding.
- Ask when requirements are ambiguous; check "Known gaps / TBD" in
  `001_CLANKER_INIT.md` before inventing architecture.
